{
  "id": "05092_doui",
  "headword": "{同意|どうい}",
  "reading": "どうい",
  "part_of_speech": "noun / suru-verb",
  "gloss": "agreement, consent",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "agreement, consent, approval",
      "explanation": "The act of agreeing with someone or giving permission; sharing the same opinion."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "05092_doui_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{意見|いけん}に{同意|どうい}する。",
      "english": "I agree with his opinion.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05092_doui_ex2",
      "japanese": "{同意|どうい}なしにデータを{使用|しよう}することはできない。",
      "english": "Data cannot be used without consent.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05092_doui_ex3",
      "japanese": "{同意|どうい}を{得|え}てから{契約|けいやく}を{結|むす}ぶ。",
      "english": "We will sign the contract after obtaining consent.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{同意|どうい} means both \"agreement\" (sharing the same opinion) and \"consent\" (giving permission). Composed of {同|どう} (same) + {意|い} (intention).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {同意|どうい}する: to agree, to consent\n- {同意|どうい}を{得|え}る: to obtain consent\n- {同意|どうい}{書|しょ}: consent form\n- {同意|どうい}なく: without consent\n- 〜に{同意|どうい}する: to agree to/with ~\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {合意|ごうい}: mutual agreement (emphasizes both parties agreeing together)\n- {賛成|さんせい}: approval, support (for a proposal or plan)\n- {承諾|しょうだく}: consent, acceptance (responding to a request — more formal)\n- {同感|どうかん}: sharing the same feeling (\"I feel the same way\")\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral to formal. {同意|どうい}{書|しょ} (consent form) is common in medical and legal contexts.",
